# Phase V3-7 CRLF/LF fix: v3/hash.py's code_hash (and V1's/V2's own
# hash_files()-based integrity hashes) hash raw file bytes directly
# (common/hashing.py::hash_files(), unmodified - see that module's own
# docstring), bypassing git's own diff/status-level CRLF normalization.
# A Frozen Model trained on this Windows machine (core.autocrlf=true,
# which re-materializes CRLF line endings for any *.py file that gets
# checked out, even though the stored git blob itself is LF) produced a
# code_hash that then genuinely differed, byte-for-byte, from the SAME
# blob checked out on GitHub Actions' ubuntu-latest runner (which does
# not perform this conversion) - a real, reproducible cross-platform
# discrepancy, not a code/recipe change (git diff/status show zero
# difference for the affected file). Forcing every checkout, on every
# platform, to always materialize Python source as LF removes the
# discrepancy at its root without touching the hash algorithm itself.
*.py text eol=lf
